==English==
===Etymology===
{{prefix|ecto|plasm}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛktəˌplæzəm/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{context|parapsychology|lang=en}} The [[visible]] [[substance]] believed to [[emanate]] from the body of a [[spiritualistic]] [[medium]] during [[communication]] with the [[dead]].
# {{context|parapsychology|lang=en}} An [[immaterial]] or [[ethereal]] substance, especially the [[transparent]] [[corporeal]] presence of a spirit or [[ghost]].
# {{context|cytology|lang=en}} The outer [[granule]]-free layer of [[cytoplasm]].

